activation	Print prompt	2026-10-28T01:16:43.8266782Z {"title": "duckdb ui fails query on variant data type", "body": "### What happens?\n\nI can create a table with a variant data type and query it using the client. trying to query the same table using the same query in the duckdb ui results in an error:\n\n```\nError: unrecognized type id: 109\n```\n\nrunning duchdb:\n\n```\nduckdb -ui -storage-version latest test6.db\n```\n\n```\nCREATE TABLE test_variant (v VARIANT);\n\nINSERT INTO test_variant VALUES\n    (42::VARIANT),\n    ('hello'::VARIANT),\n    ([1, 2, 3]::VARIANT),\n    ({'name': 'Alice'}::VARIANT);\n\nSELECT * FROM test_variant;\n```\n\nThe storage-version are:\nstorage-versions:\n```\nSELECT database_name, tags\nFROM duckdb_databases();\n\ndatabase_name    tags\nmem_db_for_profiling_queries\t{}\nlocalmemdb\t{}\n_duckdb_ui\t{storage_version=v1.5.0+}\ntest6\t{storage_version=v1.5.0+}\nsystem\t{}\ntemp\t{}\n```\n\n\n### To Reproduce\n\nno files required\n\n### OS:\n\naarch64\n\n### DuckDB Version:\n\n1.5.5\n\n### DuckDB Client:\n\nterminal\n\n### Hardware:\n\n_No response_\n\n### Full Name:\n\nUwe Geercken\n\n### Affiliation:\n\n-\n\n### Did you include all relevant configuration (e.g., CPU architecture, Linux distribution) to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all code required to reproduce the issue?\n\n- [x] Yes, I have\n\n### Did you include all relevant data sets for reproducing the issue?\n\nNot applicable - the reproduction does not require a data set"}
